From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:41:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: a Metal command buffer of its own only for render passes
 with pre_gfx work

STEAMAC-G. 0044 started every render encoder that followed other encoders in
a Metal command buffer of its own, so that the pre_gfx pass (unroll kernels,
draw predicates) of its draws could be committed right before it. A Metal
command buffer costs GPU time of its own (~55 us on an M1 Max): Steam's web
helper's command buffer of 77 blits (vk_meta: a render pass each) took
12.6 ms instead of 6.5 ms with 0042, its longest one 13.6 ms instead of 7.0.

Render encoders now start a Metal command buffer only in renderings whose
draws recorded pre_gfx work, and the pre_gfx pass goes at the end of the Metal
command buffer the render encoder started after (kept open with the pool's
other allocator until the render encoder ends), not into a third one; a
render encoder that is the first of its Metal command buffer still gets one
of its own committed before it. A rendering's first render encoder starts at
its first use when it would follow other encoders: the pre_gfx work of the
first draw goes ahead of it into the Metal command buffer being encoded (it
takes the attachments' load actions then; a rendering without draws starts
it at its end, a color attachment map change before it). A rendering whose
first pre_gfx work comes after its render encoder started behind other
encoders ends that once (as before 0044 for every such draw), its next render
encoder starts a Metal command buffer. Deferred writes after a render encoder and
timestamp writes no longer count as pre_gfx work. Command buffer records (MESA_KK_DEBUG=cbs,
queue errors) count their Metal command buffers.

host/moltenvk/repro provoking_last.c 5: a clear, 8 blits and 8 render passes
of direct draws in one command buffer: one Metal command buffer (0044: one per
render pass after the first),
1.7 ms of GPU time (0001-0045: 2.2-4.3 ms, 0001-0042: 1.7 ms); indexed draws
2 Metal command buffers, 1 render pass.
